# Environment
# `.env*` covers every variant (`.env.production`, `.env.staging`, …), not
# just the ones listed below: the backend loads `.env` from the repo root, so a
# stray `.env.production` would otherwise be committed. `.env.example` is kept.
.env
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

